            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for the air, then the Russian for a TV channel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: источник",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "источник (istóchnik) — \"a source; a spring\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Журналист не назвал свой источник. Zhurnalíst ne nazvál svoy istóchnik. The journalist did not name his source."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First sense: a spring of water. Источник информации — a source of information."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "источник (istóchnik) is built on истечь \"to flow out\", from из- \"out\" and the Slavic verb течь \"to flow\": first a spring, then any source. EtymDB lists no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
